{
  "count": 84,
  "cues": [
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-01",
      "start": 1.8,
      "end": 3.393291666666667,
      "text": "A lion's body."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-02",
      "start": 3.6932916666666666,
      "end": 5.182625,
      "text": "A woman's face."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-03",
      "start": 5.482625,
      "end": 7.455916666666666,
      "text": "Wings folded on her back."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-04",
      "start": 7.755916666666667,
      "end": 12.161208333333335,
      "text": "She watches over the city of Thebes,\nand asks its people a riddle."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-05",
      "start": 12.461208333333333,
      "end": 15.350541666666667,
      "text": "Those who cannot answer, she destroys."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-06",
      "start": 15.650541666666667,
      "end": 18.233833333333333,
      "text": "This is the Sphinx of Greek legend."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-07",
      "start": 18.533833333333334,
      "end": 21.281067765567766,
      "text": "Yet the most famous sphinx in the world,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-07",
      "start": 21.281067765567766,
      "end": 24.783791666666666,
      "text": "the great one in Egypt,\nnever asked anyone a riddle."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-08",
      "start": 25.083791666666666,
      "end": 27.00575,
      "text": "It is not even a woman."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P02-01",
      "start": 27.933333333333334,
      "end": 33.440666666666665,
      "text": "In this episode, we look at two very\ndifferent sphinxes, the guardian of Egypt"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P02-01",
      "start": 33.440666666666665,
      "end": 38.44733333333333,
      "text": "and the riddler of Greece, and at how\none name came to cover them both."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-01",
      "start": 44.3,
      "end": 47.979,
      "text": "The Great Sphinx of Giza\nwas carved from the living rock"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-01",
      "start": 47.979,
      "end": 51.657999999999994,
      "text": "of the desert, about four\nand a half thousand years ago."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-02",
      "start": 51.958,
      "end": 57.22533333333333,
      "text": "Many scholars link it to King Khafre,\nwhose pyramid rises behind it."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-03",
      "start": 57.52533333333333,
      "end": 60.822625,
      "text": "Its face wears the royal\nheadcloth of a pharaoh."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-04",
      "start": 61.122625,
      "end": 63.60791666666667,
      "text": "Its body is a lion at rest."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-01",
      "start": 64.53333333333333,
      "end": 67.97769230769231,
      "text": "In Egypt, the lion stood\nfor power, and the sphinx"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-01",
      "start": 67.97769230769231,
      "end": 70.92999999999999,
      "text": "joined that power to the face of the king."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-02",
      "start": 71.23,
      "end": 76.56133333333334,
      "text": "Sphinxes lined the roads to temples\nand kept watch over sacred places."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-03",
      "start": 76.86133333333333,
      "end": 78.868625,
      "text": "Most of them show a king."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-04",
      "start": 79.16862499999999,
      "end": 84.34753972868216,
      "text": "Hatshepsut, a woman who ruled as pharaoh,\nappears here as a sphinx too,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-04",
      "start": 84.34753972868216,
      "end": 88.712625,
      "text": "with the royal headcloth\nand the ceremonial beard of a king."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P05-01",
      "start": 89.63333333333334,
      "end": 93.49395833333334,
      "text": "We do not know what the builders\nof Giza called their sphinx."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P05-02",
      "start": 93.79395833333334,
      "end": 98.012234186747,
      "text": "More than a thousand years\nlater, Egyptians worshipped"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P05-02",
      "start": 98.012234186747,
      "end": 102.38969026104418,
      "text": "it as a god, Horemakhet,\n\"Horus in the Horizon.\" Between"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P05-02",
      "start": 102.38969026104418,
      "end": 107.00591666666668,
      "text": "its paws stands a stone set up\nby King Thutmose the Fourth."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P05-03",
      "start": 107.30591666666668,
      "end": 112.39258333333333,
      "text": "It tells how, as a young prince, he\nrested in the shadow of the great god."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P05-04",
      "start": 112.69258333333335,
      "end": 115.63078645833335,
      "text": "In a dream, the god\npromised him the kingdom,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P05-04",
      "start": 115.63078645833335,
      "end": 119.10320833333334,
      "text": "and said that the sand\nof the desert had reached him."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-01",
      "start": 122.06666666666666,
      "end": 126.06533333333333,
      "text": "In these Egyptian statues\nand stones, there is no riddle."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-02",
      "start": 126.36533333333333,
      "end": 129.170625,
      "text": "The sphinx here does not test travelers."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-03",
      "start": 129.47062499999998,
      "end": 131.55191666666667,
      "text": "It guards kings and gods."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P07-01",
      "start": 134.0,
      "end": 136.614625,
      "text": "In Greece, the sphinx was something else."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P07-02",
      "start": 136.914625,
      "end": 142.210593503937,
      "text": "The poet Hesiod, writing around\n700 BC, lists her among a family"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P07-02",
      "start": 142.210593503937,
      "end": 147.590625,
      "text": "of monsters, and calls her the destroyer\nof the people of Thebes."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P07-03",
      "start": 147.890625,
      "end": 151.19795833333333,
      "text": "In this passage, he says\nnothing about a riddle."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P08-01",
      "start": 152.1,
      "end": 155.93959523809522,
      "text": "Greek artists usually gave\nthe sphinx a woman's head,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P08-01",
      "start": 155.93959523809522,
      "end": 158.81929166666666,
      "text": "a lion's body, and the wings of a bird."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P08-02",
      "start": 159.11929166666667,
      "end": 163.81191666666666,
      "text": "Often they set her on top of a grave\nmarker, watching over the dead."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P08-03",
      "start": 164.11191666666667,
      "end": 169.55991666666665,
      "text": "This sphinx once crowned a grave\nin Attica, around 530 BC."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P09-01",
      "start": 172.2,
      "end": 174.61262499999998,
      "text": "Where the name came from is uncertain."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P09-02",
      "start": 174.912625,
      "end": 178.5416735436893,
      "text": "Some link it to a Greek\nword meaning \"to squeeze\""
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P09-02",
      "start": 178.5416735436893,
      "end": 182.6999583333333,
      "text": "or \"to bind.\" Others have\nlooked for an Egyptian origin."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P09-03",
      "start": 182.99995833333332,
      "end": 184.83658333333332,
      "text": "No one knows for sure."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-01",
      "start": 187.2,
      "end": 190.7647632352941,
      "text": "The riddle belongs\nto the stories of Thebes,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-01",
      "start": 190.7647632352941,
      "end": 194.246625,
      "text": "told on the stage\nin Athens in the 400s BC."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-02",
      "start": 194.54662499999998,
      "end": 199.71485902255637,
      "text": "In Sophocles' play Oedipus the King,\nthe people remember \"the riddling"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-02",
      "start": 199.71485902255637,
      "end": 204.50858333333332,
      "text": "Sphinx,\" and Oedipus is the stranger\nwho freed the city from her."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-03",
      "start": 204.80858333333333,
      "end": 208.15591666666666,
      "text": "Painters have returned\nto this meeting ever since."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-01",
      "start": 211.66666666666666,
      "end": 214.622625,
      "text": "But the play never gives\nthe words of the riddle."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-02",
      "start": 214.92262499999998,
      "end": 218.42058055555555,
      "text": "We find them in later\nwriters, such as Athenaeus,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-02",
      "start": 218.42058055555555,
      "end": 221.48129166666666,
      "text": "and a handbook of myths\ncalled the Library."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-03",
      "start": 221.78129166666665,
      "end": 227.47991666666667,
      "text": "They ask: what has one voice, and becomes\nfour-footed, two-footed, and three-footed?"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-04",
      "start": 227.77991666666665,
      "end": 230.12854166666665,
      "text": "The answer is a human being."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-05",
      "start": 230.42854166666666,
      "end": 234.681875,
      "text": "A baby crawls, an adult walks,\nand the old lean on a staff."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-06",
      "start": 234.981875,
      "end": 238.98116666666667,
      "text": "In these texts, there is no\nmorning, noon, or evening."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-07",
      "start": 239.28116666666665,
      "end": 241.3531159188034,
      "text": "And when the riddle was solved,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-07",
      "start": 241.3531159188034,
      "end": 244.49445833333334,
      "text": "the Library says, the Sphinx\nthrew herself down."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-01",
      "start": 250.2,
      "end": 252.81329166666666,
      "text": "So how did one name come to mean both?"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-02",
      "start": 253.11329166666667,
      "end": 255.042625,
      "text": "We do not know every step."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-03",
      "start": 255.342625,
      "end": 257.0839583333333,
      "text": "But the Greek name stayed."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-04",
      "start": 257.38395833333334,
      "end": 261.7975326190476,
      "text": "When the historian Herodotus,\nin the 400s BC, described"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-04",
      "start": 261.7975326190476,
      "end": 266.7832369047619,
      "text": "the great statues a king set up\nat a temple in Sais, in Egypt,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-04",
      "start": 266.7832369047619,
      "end": 271.68720833333333,
      "text": "he called them androsphinxes,\nsphinxes with the heads of men."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-05",
      "start": 271.98720833333334,
      "end": 276.70254166666666,
      "text": "And we still call the guardian of Giza\nby the name of a Greek monster."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P13-01",
      "start": 278.8333333333333,
      "end": 281.11929166666664,
      "text": "Its face carries another story."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P13-02",
      "start": 281.41929166666665,
      "end": 285.9712916666667,
      "text": "It is often said that Napoleon's\nsoldiers shot off its nose."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P13-03",
      "start": 286.2712916666666,
      "end": 290.2099514492753,
      "text": "Yet drawings by the Danish\ntraveler Frederic Norden,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P13-03",
      "start": 290.2099514492753,
      "end": 295.1525833333333,
      "text": "who visited in the 1730s, already\nshow the face without its nose."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P13-04",
      "start": 295.45258333333334,
      "end": 301.89191666666665,
      "text": "They were printed long before\nNapoleon came to Egypt in 1798."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-01",
      "start": 302.8,
      "end": 305.0746666666667,
      "text": "So, did the Sphinx ask riddles?"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-02",
      "start": 305.37466666666666,
      "end": 308.44733333333335,
      "text": "The Greek one did,\nin the stories of Thebes."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-03",
      "start": 308.74733333333336,
      "end": 312.39372813531355,
      "text": "The Egyptian one, far older,\nwas a king in the shape"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-03",
      "start": 312.39372813531355,
      "end": 315.96862500000003,
      "text": "of a lion, keeping watch\nat the edge of the desert."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-04",
      "start": 316.268625,
      "end": 318.2219166666667,
      "text": "Two creatures, one name."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-05",
      "start": 318.5219166666667,
      "end": 320.83925,
      "text": "Every story has an origin."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-06",
      "start": 321.13925,
      "end": 324.30720833333334,
      "text": "Sometimes, two stories\nshare the same name."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P15-01",
      "start": 328.8333333333333,
      "end": 333.99266666666665,
      "text": "This video is based on historical\ntexts and public museum collections."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P15-02",
      "start": 334.29266666666666,
      "end": 337.24923809523807,
      "text": "The narration uses synthetic speech,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P15-02",
      "start": 337.24923809523807,
      "end": 341.1913333333333,
      "text": "and some images are\nAI-generated reconstructions."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P15-03",
      "start": 341.49133333333333,
      "end": 345.4473333333333,
      "text": "Sources and terms of use are\nlisted in the description."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P15-04",
      "start": 345.7473333333333,
      "end": 348.51620634920636,
      "text": "If you enjoyed this story, please like"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P15-04",
      "start": 348.51620634920636,
      "end": 351.868,
      "text": "the video and subscribe\nfor more quiet origins."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P15-05",
      "start": 352.168,
      "end": 353.94062499999995,
      "text": "Thank you for watching."
    }
  ],
  "timing": "Exact synthesized sentence boundaries; within-sentence pages weighted by text length",
  "script_matches_ignoring_layout_whitespace": true
}
